# Assigning SELinux security contexts (or labels) to the files within the APEX which most
# importantly contain the SELinux type. SELinux types allows the definition of SELinux policies for
# these files.
# The paths are relative to the APEX's directory.
# The labels are in format user:role:type:sensitivity. Where, in Android, user is always u, role can
# be object_r or r, type can be defined and used in SELinux policy files, and sensitivity is always
# s0. For mor detail see
# https://source.android.com/docs/security/features/selinux/concepts#security_contexts
(/.*)?                u:object_r:system_file:s0
